Aardman Animations is celebrating turning 50 with a documentary special on the BBC .

"Cracking Job Gromit: Aardman at 50" &#x2014;&#xA0;due to air over Christmas &#x2014;&#xA0;will mark half a century since Morph first appeared on screens in 1976 and will chart the beloved stop-motion studio from the early adventures of "Wallace & Gromit" to "Shaun the Sheep" and "Chicken Run." Special never-before-seen footage and all new animations will feature, alongside rare archive material including early sketches, character designs and development artwork. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories Netflix’s Hit French Action Thriller ‘Elite Force’ Starring Tomer Sisley Starts Production on Season 2 'Dune: Prophecy' Star Tabu Joins YRF Entertainment's Netflix Rescue Drama 'Tunnel Men' (EXCLUSIVE)

Among the famous fans and collaborators due to appear are Lenny Henry, Romesh Ranganathan, Nick Mohammed, Amelia Dimoldenberg, Thandiwe Newton, Rob Brydon, Lauren Patel, Ben Whitehead and Jordan Stephens.

&#x201C;We&#x2019;re delighted to bring this fantastic celebration of Aardman&#x2019;s extraordinary five-decade long legacy to BBC audiences this Christmas," said Jasmyn McGuile, the BBC&#x2019;s commissioning editor for factual entertainment and events says. "With exclusive access, remarkable archive, much-loved characters, and contributions from some of the best talent in the business, it&#x2019;s a joyful tribute to one of Britain&#x2019;s most influential creative studios and a perfect festive treat for viewers of all ages.&#x201D;

Added Ed Sleeman, managing director, Mitre Studios says: "Aardman is one of the true jewels of British creativity, and getting to tell the story of their first 50 years is exactly the kind of ambitious, culturally significant storytelling we set out to do. This film celebrates not just the icons - Wallace & Gromit, Shaun the Sheep, Morph - but the extraordinary craft and people behind them. We couldn't be prouder to bring this milestone to the BBC.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Cracking Job Gromit: Aardman at 50 was commissioned for BBC One and BBC iPlayer by Jasmin McGuile and Michael Jochnowitz. Commissioning Editors for the BBC are Jasmin McGuile and Michael Jochnowitz. Executive Producers for Mitre Studios are Ed Sleeman and Jack Shillaker, the Director is Yemi Bamiro, the Producer is Samora Tikly and the Line Producer is Storm Stewart.

&#x201C;Whereas the beautiful is limited, the sublime is limitless.&#x201D;

Philosopher Immanuel Kant published this in his seminal 1781 text &#x201C;Critique of Pure Reason,&#x201D; and it&#x2019;s amazing he had such insight 245 years before he could throw an iguana in the face of a disorderly driver in &#x201C; Grand Theft Auto VI .&#x201D;

The game, now available from Rockstar, approached $4 billion in sales on its launch day and has already had a seismic impact on pop culture. It presents an absolutely enormous open and free world, making Leonida, a lightly fictionalized version of Florida, a playground for murder, chaos and carjacking. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories Malaysian War Drama 'The Ghost and the Gun' Sets Global Netflix Release (EXCLUSIVE) Netflix Partnering With BBC to to Bring Preschool Shows to Streamer, Fund New Commissions

The primary narrative is the love story of Jason and Lucia and their descent into the local crime scene. It&#x2019;s compelling and emotional, with action-packed missions coming from the jump. Consider the first proper challenge, &#x201C;Gone Fishing&#x201D;: After boating around to pick up dropped packages, you must rescue your contact from the clutches of hillbillies who live on a &#x201C;Tiger King&#x201D;-esque compound. You can either stealthily move through the patchy foliage and quietly knock out your foes, or come in guns blazing, stealing vehicles and running folks down on the property. A brilliant score, courtesy of French electronic duo Justice, punctuates the most stressful moments, and only once you escape in a seaplane does your heart stop beating. This is all before you&#x2019;re fully taught the function of the buttons on your controller.

It evokes a thrilling set-piece from a Michael Bay movie, and it's one of over 90 main missions, ranging from death-defying ambulance hijackings and shark attacks to rogue excavator demolitions and ticking-clock armed robberies. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Not only is the scale vast, but the specifics are treated reverentially. Be it the swampy backwoods or the neon-drenched city lights, Leonida is unmistakably built around the lore of the &#x201C;Florida Man.&#x201D; Scores of non-playable characters swarm the neighborhoods, with unique body shapes and quips alike. The radio is filled with retro hits, original music that evokes &#x201C;Miami Vice&#x201D;-era swagger, and endless talk from a murderer&#x2019;s row of comic minds like Janelle James, Sarah Sherman, Jason Sudeikis and &#x201C;Weird Al&#x201D; Yankovic.

Even the mild modifications from &#x201C;GTA 5&#x201D; add challenges that don&#x2019;t disrupt the fun but rather urge the player to be a bit more clever. Not every car can be hot-wired instantly; some take time to create a spark with the wires, while newer models won&#x2019;t budge without a fob. How needlessly violent you are influences the story tree and might lead to dire consequences for the lovebirds. Even a slightly tougher shooting system encourages patience and skill over blind mayhem.

Beyond the brilliantly staged missions, it cannot be overstated how the freedom to do anything on the colossal open map allows for astounding adventures and fun. Crime sprees aside, Jason and Lucia can work out, play basketball, putt at mini golf, shoot pool, race drones, go parachuting, shop, go hunting, fire at the shooting range and dozens of other activities. Your life is a movie, and you&#x2019;re the auteur. Sure, AI can spit out a junky-looking scene from a prompt, but &#x201C;GTA 6&#x201D; truly democratizes a cinematic canvas.

Spend the day doing upkeep on your home and punctuate it with stabbing, &#xE0; la Chantal Akerman&#x2019;s masterpiece &#x201C;Jeanne Dielman, 23 quai du Commerce, 1080 Bruxelles.&#x201D; Fending off an outrageously large crab attack feels like a surreal, Southern-fried homage to Denis Villeneuve&#x2019;s &#x201C;Enemy.&#x201D; The most destructive can engage in their own &#x201C;Purge.&#x201D; Hell, stage a sequel to Harmony Korine&#x2019;s &#x201C;Spring Breakers&#x201D; well before Bella Thorne gets hers off the ground.

But what does this limitless gameplay add up to beyond a choose-your-own-adventure for rifle-toting louts? In the 13 years since &#x201C;Grand Theft Auto 5&#x201D; was released, we&#x2019;ve had a cultural sea change wherein the &#x201C;greed is good&#x201D; ethos of the &#x2019;80s has come roaring back: Billionaires are deified, even as workers jockey for bathroom breaks; politicians advocate for eschewing societal norms and conduct in order to get ahead; and AI anxiety has made it unclear if a waning job market will ever recover. blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-articleX-uid2' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["btf","mid-articleX","mid"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-articleX") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[620,366]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Yet the world of &#x201C;Grand Theft Auto VI&#x201D; offers unique control. The American Dream seems increasingly distant, as you pull yourself up by your bootstraps and never prosper, but there&#x2019;s a draw in living out your dreams in a pristine simulation of real life. As the scales get tilted, taking destiny into your hands &#x2014;&#xA0;legal or not &#x2014;&#xA0;becomes increasingly appealing.

Conservative commenters dinged the game for inspiring people to skip work and glorifying violence to kids. Yet the storytelling serves a purpose. The fantasy of being the king of your block is alive in &#x201C;GTA 6.&#x201D; Call it a societal pressure valve, but time will tell if the adventures of Jason and Lucia will inspire real-life attempts to take the power back.

The music streaming service Tidal said Tuesday that it would ban tracks it believes are completely AI-generated starting next month, a move its leader believes &#x201C;will resonate with both artists and listeners alike.&#x201D;

The service will remove the AI tracks starting Dec. 9, making Tidal the first music streaming platform to ban AI music entirely. It comes nearly five months after Tidal said it would demonetize any AI-powered song, force those artists to label their tracks as either AI-generated or AI-assisted and ban AI songs that were associated with &#x201C;fraudulent activity,&#x201D; a category that includes songs impersonating established artists and efforts to &#x201C;deceive listeners.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-variety-article-mid-article-uid0' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid-article1","mid-articleX","mid","mid-article"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article") .addSize([[300,250],[2,2],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[320,480],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; }); Related Stories Taylor Swift's 'Law & Order: SVU' Crime Scene Evidence Board from the Emmys Goes on Display at the Paley Center (EXCLUSIVE) Taylor Swift to Perform at CMAs for the First Time in 13 Years

&#x201C;But that&#x2019;s enough, as 43% of tracks distributed to us in the last 90 days have been detected as AI-generated. Something more drastic needs to be done,&#x201D;&#xA0;wrote Robert Anderson, the Tidal Lead at parent company Block, in an X thread on Tuesday. &#x201C;We&#x2019;ll begin removing all wholly AI-generated tracks from our catalog, and you&#x2019;ll see them completely gone by the beginning of the year.&#x201D;

Anderson said that 96% of all AI-generated songs receive zero plays. The move will cleave the platform of 29 million tracks, Anderson added, and have it reject between 80,000 to 85,000 songs a day.

&#x201C;We encourage our peers to follow suit,&#x201D;&#xA0;he wrote.

The move comes as competitors such as Spotify and Apple Music continue to test approaches to combat the rise of AI-generated tracks proliferating on their platforms, many of which the services have labeled some version of &#x201C;slop&#x201D; or &#x201C;spam.&#x201D; Apple Music said it would also begin labeling AI-generated or AI-assisted tracks on its platform, while Spotify said it would label artists it deemed AI creations as an &#x201C;AI Persona.&#x201D; blogherads.adq.push(function () { blogherads .defineSlot( 'medrec', 'gpt-dsk-tab-mid-article2-uid1' ) .setTargeting( 'pos', ["mid","mid-article2","mid-articleX"] ) .setTargeting( 'viewable', 'yes' ) .setSubAdUnitPath("ros\/mid-article2") .addSize([[320,480],[300,250],[300,251],[2,4],[4,2],[620,366],[300,450]]) .setClsOptimization("minsize") ; });

Spotify said in a blog post last month it also removed 50 million slop or spam tracks from users' recommendations this year, which came after it removed 75 million of those songs from its catalog entirely. The revelation came among a number of updates regarding Spotify's efforts to combat AI spam.

&#x201C;This work isn&#x2019;t finished,&#x201D; Spotify added. &#x201C;AI moves fast, and bad actors adapt just as fast. But as AI makes music more abundant, we believe listeners will value human artistry even more. Our job is to make Spotify the place they find it.&#x201D;

