It took Michelle Randolph a full season to realize she was the comic relief.

At first, she played the part of Ainsley Norris &#x2014; the overly indulged, wildly inappropriate teenage daughter of Billy Bob Thornton&#x2019;s oil-industry fixer in Taylor Sheridan&#x2019;s Texas saga Landman &#x2014; as if she was a character in a Strindberg play.

